// @no-instantiate
// @hint redundant type annotation: `dleaf` is inferred as `{r: i32}` — remove it to lean on inference
// THE HINT IS DECLARED, NOT DELETED, and the annotation it names is the entire defect:
// `dleaf: Circle` is the ONLY nominal claim in the program, and the checker calling it
// redundant (it infers `{r: i32}`) is the disagreement this row is about. Remove it and there
// is nothing left to miscompile.
// MISCOMPILE, pinned: the only nominal claim in the program is the ANNOTATED BINDING the
// read's `??` DEFAULT names, and the container it decides was filled through an
// un-annotated PARAMETER. Ten lines, no import, no generic, no lambda, and — the reason
// this successor was chosen — NO LAYOUT TWIN ANYWHERE.
//
// `vl check` exits 0 (one redundant-annotation HINT, no errors) and is the ONLY command
// that misses it; `vl check --codegen` exits 1, `vl check --codegen --no-validate` exits 0,
// `vl build` writes the `.wasm` and exits 1, `vl run` exits 1:
//
//   the emitted module is not valid wasm … type mismatch:
//   expected (ref null $type), found (ref $type)
//
// (No byte offset quoted on purpose: it moves with the seed.)
//
// WHY THIS ONE AND NOT ANOTHER — and the selection rule is the one the genealogy in
// `tests/vl_check_codegen_test.ts` earned. Its predecessor was chosen for STABILITY against
// the pin family and was closed anyway, by a change from a different layer entirely (the
// variant⇄struct heap merge, D280). So this one is chosen for stability against BOTH: it has
// no delivery for the pin family to read, and it declares no second claimant of the arm's
// layout for the heap merge to have anything to merge. `armLayoutContested` is FALSE here,
// `variantStructHeapTwinAt` answers -1, and `uVarTwin` has no second arm to collapse — the
// three mechanisms that closed the rest of this family are each inapplicable by construction
// rather than by omission.
//
// THE ONE-LINE CONTROL, and it is the pair that names the coordinate. Move the SAME
// annotation from the read's default to the container binding —
//
//     const m: {[string]: Circle} = c
//     print((((m)["k1"] ?? { r: 0 })).r)
//
// — and the identical program RUNS on this tree and on `28425535`. That sibling is
// `silent-class-inventory.md` D173's refutation pin, which this file sits one annotation
// POSITION away from: a claim at the container is a DELIVERY the pin family reads, a claim
// at the read is a CONSUMPTION it cannot. D158 is the row that names the position; this is
// its `twin=notwin` × `storage=param` cell, and the six cells of that shape are the whole
// surviving residue of the 1,188-cell annotation-position grid (`scripts/silent-sweep/d156/`)
// after D280. Filed as D282.
//
// PRE-EXISTING on `28425535` — measured, not inherited: graded `check-clean invalid wasm` on
// that commit's own seed (1,461,851 bytes) and on this change's (1,463,065), with the same
// sentence at the same offset (1258) across the two.
//
// IT IS THE SPECIMEN. This file is kept byte-for-byte identical to
// `tests/vl_check_codegen_test.ts`'s `INVALID_MODULE_SRC` below its header, which needs a
// program that type-checks clean and whose module the engine refuses.
//
// WHEN IT IS FIXED this file starts failing (the module instantiates), which is the point:
// delete it, graduate a `@run` row, and swap `INVALID_MODULE_SRC` for another live member of
// the class. READ THE NOTE IN `tests/vl_check_codegen_test.ts` BEFORE DOING THAT — including
// what it says about where to look before concluding the class is empty. Five more live
// members are the sibling cells of this one: `read × param × d{1,2,3} × arm × notwin ×
// {norm,rev}`, which `scripts/silent-sweep/d156/gen156.py` re-derives.
type Circle = { r: i32 }
type Sq = { s: i32 }
type Shape = Circle | Sq
function fill(c, n: i32) {
  c["k1"] = { r: n }
}
const c = Map()
fill(c, 7)
const dleaf: Circle = { r: 0 }
print((((c)["k1"] ?? dleaf)).r)
